{% comment %}
  The inner wrapper is what scrolls sideways below 992px — see `.selected-scroller` in
  _sass/_base.scss. It has to be its own element because jekyll-scholar emits the
  `<ol class="bibliography">` itself, leaving nowhere else to hang these attributes.

  role + aria-label + tabindex are what axe's `scrollable-region-focusable` rule asks for:
  a box that scrolls has to be reachable and scrollable with the keyboard alone. `axe.yml`
  runs this check on every push.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="publications selected-grid">
  <div class="selected-scroller" role="region" aria-label="Selected publications" tabindex="0">
    {% bibliography --template bib_selected --group_by none --query @*[selected=true]* %}
  </div>
</div>
